The main overclaim is stronger than “detection needs gossip.” Ordinary signed calls bind selected state, not the member’s whole observed history. A writer can therefore relay applicable calls across divergent histories without making their chain hashes equal. The hash-binding theorem alone does not establish SUNDR’s no-join property for client operations.

The page scanner also has a concrete gap: it reads the final head value for every earlier touch, so a later update can replace the conflicting value before comparison.

